{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Shall one contend with Shaddai, the discipliner?</b> — The way of musar is that a person contend with Shaddai." "<b>He who reproves El shall answer it</b> — Job: that HaShem reprove him, why he does not answer to this."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "I read הרוב as 'shall one contend' following the verse; the phrase מוסר הוא may mean 'it is [the way of] musar [i.e., rebuke/discipline],' though the construction is elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:20.965003666Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}